  "secondary_categories": [],
  "slug": "high-nanoantenna-b3b2",
  "summary": "Seven preprints report quantified resonance control via strong coupling, vapor-driven anion exchange and material choice across dielectric, perovskite, plasmonic and 2D platforms.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is engineering resonant response through mode coupling, composition or environment. Silicon BIC metasurfaces use QBIC-GMR strong coupling for intrinsic circular dichroism of 0.995 at 1653.9 nm (Q = 1083). Bulk WS2 metasurfaces reach polarization-independent self-hybridized strong coupling between Brillouin-zone-folding quasi-BICs and A excitons. MAPbBr3 BIC resonances tune reversibly and continuously under HCl/HBr vapor anion exchange, and coupled TiO2 and perovskite-coated microresonators show non-monotonic whispering gallery mode hybridization. Plasmonic nanoantenna arrays with hollow-core fiber coupling report 2.1 mW THz output and 145 dB dynamic range, while a theoretical coaxial nanoantenna study maps inverse Faraday magnetization across five materials. MXene-derived TiO2 polarizers (FOM 17.5) add an integrated-photonics route. New here is the breadth of quantified tuning mechanisms; several results are numerical or theoretical.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
